:-0.10085641586515376,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.000887517032870908,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.02402,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":16.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.5,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":50.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Galaxy Digital Inc. engages in the digital asset and data centre infrastructure businesses in North America and internationally. It operates through Digital Assets, Data Centers, and Treasury and Corporate segments. The Digital Assets segment provides over-the-counter spot and derivatives trading, lending, and structured products, as well as mergers and acquisitions advisory, and equity and debt capital markets services. This segment also manages investments in the digital assets' ecosystem; and offers blockchain-centric technology and infrastructure solutions, including staking, tokenization, and custodial technology. The Data Centers segment comprises the Helios infrastructure assets. The Treasury and Corporate segment engages in managing a portfolio of digital assets, ventures, private equity, and fund investments, as well as in bitcoin mining operations. It also offers GalaxyOne, a retail financial technology platform designed for individual investors seeking access to traditional and digital markets. The company has a strategic collaboration with BNY to advance digital asset infrastructure. The company was founded in 2018 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Edward Novogratz | Founder, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 800 people. Revenue per employee of $75.5M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $67K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Galaxy Digital Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $8.4B market cap on $60.4B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at -44254% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $1.5B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -3.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 10.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (19.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 29% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 98% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Large open-market insider purchases (net $8.5M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Could Galaxy Digital (GLXY) Gain From A National Trust Bank Charter?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-glxy/galaxy-digital/news/what-could-galaxy-digital-glxy-gain-from-a-national-trust-ba","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586772.704,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.972,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Galaxy Digital (GLXY) Stock May Trade At A Discount After Tokenized Listing News","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-glxy/galaxy-digital/news/galaxy-digital-glxy-stock-may-trade-at-a-discount-after-toke","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794497028.116,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.881,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Galaxy Digital (NasdaqGS:GLXY) Dropped, So What Is Driving Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-glxy/galaxy-digital/news/galaxy-digital-nasdaqgsglxy-dropped-so-what-is-driving-atten","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794381764.942,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.802,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Douglas R. Deason Acquires 5,000 Shares of Galaxy Digital at $13.98 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/douglas-r-deason-acquires-5000-shares-of-galaxy-digital-at-1398-each","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":179